"""Direct question-design review of Ayurveda and selected religious-place niches."""
from review_angle_plans import revise_domain, audit

AYURVEDA = """history_origins|Ayurveda in Historical Sources|How did a named Ayurvedic concept change across dated texts and practice?|Compare translations, manuscript dates, and later interpretation without claiming a single origin.
famous_examples|A Widely Promoted Ayurvedic Remedy|What does the evidence establish about one frequently cited remedy for a defined outcome?|Compare the exact preparation, population, trial design, harms, and evidence quality.
hidden_stories|Patients and Practitioners in the Record|Whose experience is missing from a familiar history of Ayurvedic care?|Use consented accounts and dated institutional records without treating anecdotes as efficacy evidence.
beginner_explainers|Tradition, Product, and Clinical Claim|What different meanings does Ayurveda have in a specific care setting?|Distinguish historical framework, practitioner service, manufactured product, and testable outcome claim.
advanced_concepts|Studying a Complex Intervention|How can researchers test a multi-component Ayurvedic intervention fairly?|Define components, comparator, outcomes, follow-up, and limits to generalization.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Reported Effect With Uncertain Cause|What evidence would separate treatment effect from recovery, placebo, or selection?|Use a specified claim and examine trial quality and missing data.
technology_innovation|Testing and Tracking Preparations|Can one testing or traceability method improve the safety of Ayurvedic products?|Compare contaminant detection, batch variation, enforcement, and real-world access.
people_personalities|A Practitioner or Researcher's Influence|How did one person shape a documented Ayurvedic institution or study?|Use dated publications, institutional records, and critical responses.
major_events|A Change in Ayurvedic Regulation|What changed after one dated safety or practice rule?|Compare official rule text, implementation, inspections, and outcomes in one jurisdiction.
how_it_works|From Product Label to Safety Check|What must be checked before a product claim can be evaluated?|Map ingredient identity, dose, manufacturing, contamination, interactions, and outcome evidence.
rise_fall|A Treatment's Reputation Over Time|Why did one preparation gain or lose clinical credibility?|Track primary studies, reviews, safety notices, and changing standards.
then_vs_now|A Historical Claim and a Modern Test|How does a traditional use differ from a modern clinical efficacy claim?|Specify the historical context and the exact contemporary population and outcome.
future_developments|The Next Evidence Question|Which study would most reduce uncertainty about one Ayurvedic claim?|State comparator, sample, safety monitoring, and prerequisites without predicting success.
myths_vs_facts|Natural Does Not Establish Safety|Which safety claim about a named product survives product-specific testing?|Check contaminants, interactions, adverse events, and regulator notices.
documentary_stories|A Product Claim's Paper Trail|How did one Ayurvedic claim move from source text to modern marketing?|Trace translations, studies, labels, and regulator findings.
claim_evidence|One Claim, One Outcome|What evidence supports or weakens a specific Ayurvedic health claim?|Separate traditional rationale, laboratory results, and clinical outcomes.
care_pathway|Integrative Care Handoffs|Where can communication fail when a patient uses Ayurveda alongside conventional care?|Map disclosure, medication review, referral, and follow-up without giving treatment instructions.
benefit_harm|Benefits and Harms in One Study|What did a trial measure about both benefit and adverse effects?|Read protocol, denominators, outcomes, and reporting gaps.
mechanism_vs_outcome|Plausibility and Patient Outcomes|Does a proposed biological mechanism predict a measured clinical benefit?|Compare mechanistic work with controlled human outcomes and dose.
population_difference|Who Was Actually Studied?|Can a result in one study population apply to another?|Check age, condition, co-treatment, exclusions, and sample size.
quality_of_guidance|A Guidance Document's Evidence Base|How does one official or professional guideline grade Ayurvedic evidence?|Read recommendation, review method, safety caveats, and date.
access_to_care|Why People Seek Ayurvedic Care|Which barriers or preferences shape access to a named service?|Use consented accounts and service data without assuming efficacy.
patient_experience|A Patient's Care Journey|What can one consented patient account reveal about communication and expectations?|Separate experience, diagnosis, and clinical outcome; protect privacy.
misinformation_path|A Claim Beyond the Evidence|How did one product claim become stronger than its cited research?|Compare study population and outcome with the public claim and corrections.
prevention_boundary|Prevention Claim Versus Proven Care|Could one preventive claim delay evidence-based care for a defined condition?|Use current guidance and documented substitution risks; offer no personal advice.
system_pressure|Demand and Oversight|How does growing demand affect product quality oversight or service capacity?|Compare registrations, inspections, workforce, and reported harms in one jurisdiction.
historical_revision|Re-reading an Old Medical Text|How did translation or new archival evidence revise a familiar historical account?|Compare editions, provenance, and later clinical reinterpretation.
field_clinical_evidence|A Trial Under Examination|What can one controlled study of an Ayurvedic intervention actually establish?|Check registration, comparator, blinding, outcomes, attrition, and harms.
field_care_quality|Quality Across Providers|How is quality measured for a defined Ayurvedic service?|Compare training, documentation, referral, audit, and patient outcomes.
field_patient_safety|A Product Safety Signal|What did an official safety investigation establish about one preparation?|Read lab methods, affected batches, exposure, and regulator action.
field_health_equity|Access and Unequal Risk|Who has access to reliable information and quality-checked products?|Compare costs, language, geography, oversight, and affected voices.
field_service_capacity|A Service Under Demand|Can a named Ayurvedic service meet demand while maintaining documented safety processes?|Use staffing, caseload, referrals, and oversight data."""

PILGRIMAGE = """history_origins|A Pilgrimage Route Takes Shape|When does a named route first appear in surviving records?|Compare dated texts, maps, archaeology, and later devotional accounts.
famous_examples|A Famous Sacred Destination in Context|How did one pilgrimage site become important to different communities?|Trace attributed traditions, institutions, and visitor records across time.
hidden_stories|The People Who Sustain a Route|Whose labor keeps a pilgrimage route usable?|Document residents, guides, caretakers, transport workers, and their own accounts.
beginner_explainers|What Makes a Journey a Pilgrimage?|How do practitioners describe the purpose and obligations of one journey?|Attribute beliefs to communities and explain variation within them.
advanced_concepts|Sacred Geography and Authority|Who defines the route, access, and meaning of one sacred place?|Compare textual, institutional, and local authority in a dated setting.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Disputed Site Identification|What can evidence establish about one contested historical site identification?|Separate archaeological findings, texts, and devotional claims.
technology_innovation|Mapping a Living Route|Can a digital route map improve access without exposing sensitive sacred spaces?|Compare consent, map accuracy, privacy, and local stewardship.
people_personalities|A Route's Documented Steward|How did one named person shape a pilgrimage site or route?|Use dated records and community perspectives beyond a heroic biography.
major_events|A Pilgrimage Site Changes|How did one dated event alter access, ritual, or stewardship?|Use records before and after, including resident and practitioner voices.
how_it_works|A Journey from Home to Shrine|What practical and ritual stages do participants describe on one route?|Map local variation, travel logistics, and site protocols without prescribing worship.
rise_fall|Changing Visitor Numbers|Why did attendance rise or fall at one site over a defined period?|Compare counting methods, transport, access rules, and wider events.
then_vs_now|One Route Across Generations|What changed in travel, lodging, and ritual experience on one route?|Pair dated records with attributed living testimony.
future_developments|A Site's Capacity Choices|Which local choices could accommodate visitors while protecting the site's meaning?|Compare proposals, capacity evidence, and stakeholder views.
myths_vs_facts|Legend and Historical Claim|Which parts of a popular origin story are devotional tradition and which are documentable history?|Attribute belief and date the surviving evidence.
documentary_stories|A Pilgrimage in Records and Voices|What do route documents and participant accounts reveal about one journey?|Use consented interviews, dated records, and clear gaps.
map_vs_ground|The Route on Paper and on Foot|Where does an official route differ from locally used paths?|Compare maps, field accounts, restrictions, and terrain.
route_choices|Why Pilgrims Choose Different Paths|How do ritual preference, cost, access, and safety shape route choice?|Ask travelers and local stewards; avoid one universal itinerary.
seasonality|A Sacred Calendar and Visitor Flow|How do festival dates and weather alter demand at one site?|Compare calendars, counts, and local service capacity.
local_voice|Residents of a Sacred Place|How do nearby residents describe the benefits and costs of visitation?|Use attributed voices and disaggregated local evidence.
landscape_process|Landscape and Sacred Meaning|How has a physical landscape changed around one sacred route?|Compare maps and environmental records while attributing religious meaning.
accessibility|Who Can Reach the Site?|What mobility, cost, or language barriers affect a named pilgrimage?|Examine facilities and lived accounts with local disability perspectives.
infrastructure|Water, Waste, and Transport|Which service is under the greatest strain during peak pilgrimage?|Use seasonal demand and service data with local context.
environmental_pressure|Visitor Impact on a Sacred Landscape|What measurable environmental change is linked to visitor use?|Distinguish visitor effects from other land-use pressures.
safety_decision|A Crowd-Management Decision|What evidence informed one site's crowd or emergency policy?|Read official plans and after-action reports; avoid real-time route instructions.
place_history|A Shrine and Its Settlement|How did the site and surrounding community develop together?|Use dated land, building, and oral-history evidence.
comparison_of_places|Two Sites, Different Stewardship|How do two pilgrimage sites handle comparable visitor pressures?|Match religious context, scale, local governance, and season.
responsible_access|Access to a Living Sacred Place|How are visitor access and community protocols negotiated?|Center custodians' permissions, law, and visitor guidance.
field_route_traditions|Parallel Route Traditions|Which communities recognize different paths to the same destination?|Attribute each tradition and trace documented changes.
field_sacred_access|Who Sets Entry Rules?|How were access rules at one sacred site established and contested?|Use dated rules, legal records, and affected community voices.
field_seasonal_crowding|A Peak-Season Bottleneck|Where and when does capacity strain appear at one site?|Compare counts, flow plans, and local experience.
field_local_communities|Living Beside a Pilgrimage Route|How does the journey affect households along a specific segment?|Use consented accounts and local economic and service data.
field_visitor_infrastructure|A Facility's Real Capacity|Does one visitor facility meet peak needs fairly?|Compare design capacity, use, maintenance, and accessibility."""

TEMPLES = """history_origins|A Temple's Earliest Record|What does the earliest dated evidence establish about one temple?|Compare inscriptions, architecture, texts, and later origin narratives.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Temple Tradition|How did one well-known practice develop at a named temple?|Use dated records and practitioner accounts; avoid treating one site as universal.
hidden_stories|Caretakers Behind Temple Life|Whose work sustains daily temple practice but is absent from standard histories?|Use consented accounts of custodians, artists, and service workers.
beginner_explainers|A Temple as a Living Institution|What functions does one temple serve for its community today?|Map worship, stewardship, learning, and local variation.
advanced_concepts|Ritual Authority and Change|Who has authority to interpret or change one temple practice?|Compare lineage, institutional rules, law, and community perspectives.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Temple Date Under Debate|Which evidence supports competing dates for one temple feature?|Separate inscription, style, reuse, and later tradition.
technology_innovation|Documenting a Temple Collection|Can digital recording help preserve one collection with custodial consent?|Compare access, context, sacred restrictions, and preservation value.
people_personalities|A Temple Patron or Custodian|What did one documented figure actually contribute to a temple?|Distinguish inscriptional evidence from later biography.
major_events|A Temple's Turning Point|How did one dated event change worship, patronage, or access?|Compare records before and after and include community memory.
how_it_works|A Day of Temple Practice|How do practitioners describe a named sequence at one temple?|Attribute the local protocol and avoid prescribing observance.
rise_fall|Patronage and Temple Capacity|How did changes in resources affect one temple's functions?|Use grants, accounts, maintenance records, and local testimony.
then_vs_now|Continuity and Change in Practice|Which elements of a named practice changed across generations?|Compare dated descriptions and present practitioner voices.
future_developments|A Conservation Choice|How might one proposal affect worship and material preservation?|Compare conservation assessments and custodial priorities.
myths_vs_facts|Narrative and Material Evidence|How should a temple origin narrative be presented beside dated material evidence?|Attribute devotional accounts and state what records can establish.
documentary_stories|A Temple Through Its Records|What do inscriptions, archives, and oral histories reveal about one site?|Explain provenance, translation, gaps, and living memory.
text_source|A Text Cited at a Temple|How is one text used and interpreted in a named local practice?|Identify edition, translation, and practitioner interpretation.
interpretive_lineages|Different Readings of One Practice|How do two lineages explain the same temple practice differently?|Represent each view in its own terms with attributed sources.
lived_practice|Worship as Practiced Here|What do participants say matters in one recurring observance?|Use consented voices and specify place, community, and date.
ritual_sequence|The Order of an Observance|Which steps are public and what meanings do participants assign them?|Respect restrictions and avoid presenting local sequence as universal.
language_translation|A Temple Term in Translation|What meaning is lost when one ritual term is translated loosely?|Compare original usage, scholarly translation, and living interpretation.
regional_variants|A Practice Across Regions|How does one temple practice differ between two regions?|Compare comparable settings and explain lineage and local history.
art_and_devotion|An Image in Ritual Context|How do form, placement, and practice shape the meaning of one temple image?|Use iconographic sources and attributed devotional voices.
community_memory|Remembering a Temple Change|How do generations recount a dated change at one temple?|Compare oral accounts with records without dismissing memory.
ethics_in_context|Access and Inclusion at a Temple|How have entry or participation rules affected different people?|Use dated rules, law, and affected community testimony.
source_and_history|An Inscription's Limits|What can one inscription establish about a temple's history?|Read date, language, provenance, patronage, and omissions.
encounter_and_exchange|A Temple and Neighboring Traditions|What documented exchanges shaped one site's art or practice?|Trace specific contacts without assuming a single direction of influence.
contemporary_voice|A Present Steward's Perspective|What does a current practitioner or custodian identify as the urgent issue?|Pair consented testimony with site records and other affected voices.
field_ritual_architecture|Space Designed for Practice|How does one architectural feature support a documented ritual?|Compare plan, alterations, texts, and observed current use.
field_regional_temple_lineage|A Regional Temple Lineage|What evidence links temples in one regional tradition?|Use dated patronage, architecture, texts, and living practice.
field_inscription_context|Reading a Temple Inscription|Who commissioned one inscription and what did it seek to record?|Check original text, translation, date, and material context.
field_patronage_history|Who Funded the Temple?|How did a documented patronage change affect one temple?|Use grants, inscriptions, accounts, and later stewardship.
field_preservation_choice|Preserving a Living Site|How can a conservation decision respect worship and the building?|Compare material assessment, custodial needs, and community consultation."""

ANCIENT = """history_origins|An Ancient Tradition in Its Own Sources|What do the earliest surviving sources show about one named tradition?|Date sources and distinguish practice from later reconstruction.
famous_examples|A Famous Ancient Ritual in Context|What can evidence establish about one widely described ancient ritual?|Compare original text, archaeology, and later retellings.
hidden_stories|Ordinary Worshippers in Ancient Records|Whose participation is missing from elite accounts?|Use household finds, inscriptions, and evidence limits.
beginner_explainers|How We Know About Ancient Religion|What kinds of evidence survive for one community's religious life?|Explain texts, objects, architecture, and gaps without assuming uniform belief.
advanced_concepts|Reconstructing Practice from Fragments|How can scholars infer practice without treating one source as universal?|Compare independent evidence and alternative readings.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Deity or Site Identification in Dispute|What evidence supports competing identifications?|State uncertainty in inscription, image, date, and later interpretation.
technology_innovation|New Methods for Old Evidence|What can a new imaging or dating method reveal about one source?|Compare method, calibration, provenance, and interpretive limits.
people_personalities|A Named Ancient Participant|What can a surviving record tell us about one worshipper or patron?|Distinguish documented role from reconstructed beliefs.
major_events|A Religious Change in Dated Records|What changed after one documented political or social event?|Compare source survival and local variation before and after.
how_it_works|Reconstructing One Ceremony|Which stages of a named ancient ceremony are actually documented?|Separate contemporary record from later reconstruction.
rise_fall|Changing Visibility of a Tradition|Did practice decline, or did its records become less visible?|Compare dated evidence, preservation, and continuity.
then_vs_now|Ancient Evidence and Living Continuity|How do present communities relate to one ancient tradition?|Let living practitioners define continuity while distinguishing ancient sources.
future_developments|An Unanswered Research Question|Which new evidence could resolve a defined historical disagreement?|Specify needed excavation, edition, or provenance without predicting discovery.
myths_vs_facts|A Modern Story About Ancient Belief|Does a popular claim fit the dated evidence?|Trace the claim to source and mark later reinterpretation.
documentary_stories|One Ancient Site's Evidence Trail|How did scholars identify and reinterpret one religious site?|Follow excavation records, objects, publications, and challenges.
text_source|A Religious Text's Transmission|What can surviving copies establish about one text's history?|Compare manuscripts, language, date, and editorial choices.
interpretive_lineages|Later Readings of an Ancient Source|How have different communities read one inherited text?|Attribute each reading and distinguish historical setting.
lived_practice|Practice Beyond Written Doctrine|What evidence reveals everyday devotion in one community?|Use domestic objects, local inscriptions, and limits of inference.
ritual_sequence|A Documented Ritual Sequence|Which steps of one ancient rite are attested and by whom?|Separate prescriptions from evidence of performance.
language_translation|A Key Term Across Languages|How does translation change a religious term's apparent meaning?|Compare original-language contexts and justified translations.
regional_variants|One Tradition Across Two Regions|What differed in material and textual practice between regions?|Match periods and account for uneven surviving evidence.
art_and_devotion|An Object in Religious Context|What can an ancient image tell us about use and meaning?|Check findspot, patron, dating, and competing interpretations.
community_memory|Memory of an Ancient Place|How do later communities remember one old sacred site?|Attribute living memory and compare dated historical evidence.
ethics_in_context|Studying Sacred Remains Responsibly|Whose interests should guide access to one ancient sacred object or site?|Consider source communities, custodians, law, and provenance.
source_and_history|A Fragment and a Historical Claim|How much can one fragment support about ancient religious life?|State provenance, dating, translation, and missing context.
encounter_and_exchange|Religious Exchange at a Border|What evidence shows contact between two named traditions?|Trace objects, words, travel, and chronology without assuming borrowing.
contemporary_voice|Living Views of Ancient Heritage|How do today's related communities describe their connection to ancient material?|Use consented voices and avoid assigning identity from archaeology.
field_source_tradition|A Source's Journey to Us|How was one ancient religious text copied, translated, and preserved?|Track dated witnesses and editorial uncertainty.
field_lived_practice|An Everyday Religious Object|What does one household or local find show about use?|Read archaeological context and avoid overgeneralization.
field_regional_variation|Practice in Two Ancient Places|Which difference is supported by comparable evidence?|Align period, source type, and preservation conditions.
field_translation_issue|A Contested Ancient Word|Why do translations of one word diverge?|Compare original contexts, grammar, and interpretive stakes.
field_intercommunity_contact|Evidence of Encounter|What survives of contact between named religious communities?|Compare dated records and material evidence with careful attribution."""

if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("281", "281_ayurveda", AYURVEDA,
                  "Historical Ayurvedic traditions, clinical claim evaluation, product quality, patient safety, and care communication.",
                  "dated primary texts and translations, registered trials, systematic reviews, current clinical guidance, regulator notices, and consented accounts",
                  "Attribute traditional explanations; distinguish clinical evidence from belief, laboratory findings, and anecdotes. Give no diagnosis or treatment advice; verify product-specific safety and current guidance.")
    revise_domain("075", "075_pilgrimage_sacred_places", PILGRIMAGE,
                  "Sacred journeys as living traditions, routes, access, local stewardship, infrastructure, and environmental pressure.",
                  "dated texts and maps, site and access rules, heritage records, visitor data, environmental assessments, and consented local and practitioner accounts",
                  "Attribute sacred claims to communities; distinguish devotional narrative from dated historical evidence. Respect site protocols and verify current local access and safety information.")
    revise_domain("276", "276_temple_traditions", TEMPLES,
                  "Temple practice, interpretation, inscriptions, architecture, patronage, access, and stewardship across distinct communities.",
                  "original and translated texts, dated inscriptions, conservation records, site rules, archives, and consented practitioner and custodian accounts",
                  "Attribute beliefs and local protocols; distinguish source tradition from independently dated history. Respect restricted practice and avoid treating one lineage as universal.")
    revise_domain("289", "289_ancient_religions", ANCIENT,
                  "Ancient religious evidence, interpretation, regional variation, transmission, and living relationships to heritage.",
                  "dated archaeological reports, primary texts and manuscript witnesses, inscriptions, provenance records, translations, and consented community accounts",
                  "State gaps and disputed interpretations; avoid presenting ancient traditions as uniform or automatically extinct. Let living communities describe their own continuity.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
